{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1133597-orpheus-spectre-health","id":1133597,"title":"Orpheus Spectre 'Health'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-24T17:22:16-07:00","id":1133597,"title":"Orpheus Spectre 'Health'","content":"So, I understand that in the Orpheus game line bashing removes one 'vitality' and lethal removes two. PCs have the option to tap Spite or a Spite Rating to get back Vitality. In the case of Spectres I am having trouble figuring out if they have more than willpower points and thievery to 'heal' with. Can they somehow tap their Spite to regain it as well? Sounds weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11884-gordona8","name":"Gordona8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T04:57:08-07:00","id":1133735,"title":"","content":"Very weird, and I'd hesitate to give Spectre's an infinite pool of power to play with, which is how letting them tap Spite would play out. <br /> <br /> Considering the mentality and modus operandi of the Spectres, though, it actually makes sense that they wouldn't put as much emphasis on self preservation. It's entirely reasonable that they have a harder time healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T22:06:01-07:00","id":1138499,"title":"","content":"Spectres don't tap Spite the same way non-Spectres do. When a Spectre takes damage or taps Spite, the points are effectively &quot;spent&quot; for the scene. The downside to this is that they don't have as big a &quot;health&quot; pool to play with (but I've found that to be a good thing---with Willpower to refresh their Spite, the PCs already have a LOT of health to burn through to destroy a Spectre). There's a big advantage to this, however: The Spectre regains *all* of their Spite when the scene is finished. So, a nearly-defeated Spectre who escapes can quickly return, fully healed (less any Willpower they expended).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}